WEBVTT

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:02.770
Good work, team!

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:07.440
I Don't Want to Lose

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:06.890
It was a close battle, but you pulled through.

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:10.360
Getting into the third round 
is an amazing feat!

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:13.570
It'd be nice if we could savor 
this victory for a little longer,

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:16.870
Mifune Dolphins

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:16.870
Coach   Fujii

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:16.870
Mifune Dolphins

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:16.870
Manager  Tashiro

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:17.200
but our third-round match 
starts right after lunch.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:18.940
Make sure you're ready for it!

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:19.880
Yes, sir!

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:23.680
Manager, who are we playing 
in our third-round game?

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:27.990
Whoever wins out of the Hongou Sharks 
and the Shimizu Iron Boys.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.800
Do we have any data on either of them?

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:32.050
Nope!

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:37.550
Suzuki Andy

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:37.550
Urabe Hayato

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:36.470
I think it's reasonable to 
assume the Sharks will win.

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:37.550
Yeah.

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:39.120
You know of them?

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.920
We heard the name back 
when we were in Touto.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:45.640
They tend to finish in 
the top four every year.

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:50.700
They started their second-round game 
the same time we did, over on Field B.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.360
They might still be playing.

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:54.360
Guess we can go over and 
see them in action, then.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:55.740
Yeah!

00:00:58.530 --> 00:00:59.590
Daigo!

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:04.450
Gramps! Grandma!

00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:06.130
Thanks for coming to watch me play.

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:08.280
You were pretty good out there!

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:10.290
You played well, Dai-chan!

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:12.460
Y-You think so?

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:16.370
We can't stay for your 
afternoon game, but go get 'em.

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:18.810
Remember, the catcher is 
the linchpin of the team!

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:19.890
Do your best.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:21.080
I will!

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:01.610
Hongou

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:01.610
Shimizu

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:05.620
11–0. They called the game in the fifth...

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:10.590
Due to the consecutive pitching 
restrictions, we won't face that pitcher,

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.750
but their offense will be a handful.

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:18.760
Satou Hikaru

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:14.780
<i>They were really good.</i>

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:18.760
<i>I don't think they'd hit
Hikaru's pitches so easily, though.</i>

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:23.010
Manager, who's our starting catcher 
going to be in our next game?

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:25.780
Good question.

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:28.550
How's your leg holding up, Andy?

00:03:28.990 --> 00:03:33.150
We didn't get you batting last game, 
but running would be difficult, wouldn't it?

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:34.970
Yeah, probably.

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:37.800
Given our situation,
we shouldn't care about base running.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:40.950
We now know Shigeno isn't ready to start,

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:42.110
so you're our only hope.

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:46.620
That's all well and good, Urabe, 
but if my injury flares up again,

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:51.060
I won't be able to turn out against the 
Touto Boys next week even if we win today.

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:54.380
Satou will be our starting pitcher.

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:57.140
His catcher should be 
someone he works best with.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:03.190
I agree.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:06.710
We'll go with Satou and Shigeno 
as our battery in the third round.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:08.180
I'm counting on you, Daigo!

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:09.920
Yes, sir!

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:12.770
Ariyoshi

00:04:10.570 --> 00:04:12.770
If we win the next game, 
we're in the quarterfinals!

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:14.580
Hey, we're pretty amazing, aren't we?

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:18.230
Nagai

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:16.640
Maybe we should start 
bragging to our friends.

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:21.530
All right, team, start warming up!

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:22.240
Yes, sir!

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:27.270
Um, Manager?

00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:27.830
Hm?

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:30.660
Can I... have a word?

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:36.650
You said you'd make sure 
I got some game time.

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:40.210
I didn't get to play at all in the last game.

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:41.480
I'm really sorry.

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:43.550
There wasn't a good time to swap you in.

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:45.130
But...

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:49.620
I do intend on starting you out in 
right field in our next game, though.

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:52.110
I'm counting on you, Nagai.

00:04:52.570 --> 00:04:54.190
Ah, yes, sir!

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:58.270
Hey, is that a good idea?

00:04:58.980 --> 00:04:59.820
Sure.

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:03.110
It's not like I'm putting him in out of pity.

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:06.680
The Sharks have a strong offense, 
and when it comes to defending the outfield,

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:08.570
I actually have more faith in Nagai.

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:12.290
He never stopped putting in
 the hours in training, either.

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:15.290
Batting first, shortstop, Kimura.

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:18.790
Shortstop

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:18.790
Kimura

00:05:15.470 --> 00:05:16.230
Yes, sir!

00:05:16.630 --> 00:05:18.110
Batting second, catcher, Shigeno.

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:18.790
Yes, sir!

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:20.810
Batting third, left field, Urabe.

00:05:20.810 --> 00:05:21.500
Yes, sir.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:23.310
Batting fourth, pitcher, Satou.

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:23.920
Yes, sir!

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:25.840
Batting fifth, third base, Ariyoshi.

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:26.550
Yes, sir!

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:29.180
Center field

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:29.180
Kishimoto

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:28.530
Batting sixth, center field, Kishimoto.

00:05:28.530 --> 00:05:29.180
Yes, sir!

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:34.680
Second base

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:34.680
Katsumata

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:34.680
First base

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:34.680
Matsubara

00:05:29.670 --> 00:05:31.290
Batting seventh, first base, Matsubara.

00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:32.320
Yes, sir!

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:34.090
Batting eighth, second base, Katsumata.

00:05:34.090 --> 00:05:34.680
Yes, sir!

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:37.490
Batting ninth, right field, Nagai.

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:39.310
Yes, sir!

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:43.690
Sakura Mutsuko

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:43.690
Tsuburaya

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:43.690
Takahashi

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:42.650
Sakura, Andy, Takahashi, and Tsuburaya
make up our bench.

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:43.690
That's everything.

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:45.450
Looks like you got in, Nagai.

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:46.830
Awesome!

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:50.240
That's where real skills get you. <i>Skills.</i>

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:51.240
Huh?

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:55.250
Okay, fly balls coming up!

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:56.510
Center field!

00:05:57.570 --> 00:05:59.020
Got it!

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:01.010
Nice catch!

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:03.170
<i>Just wait and see.</i>

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:07.800
<i>I'll show you that I'm way better 
than that beginner, Sakura!</i>

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.430
Next up, right field!

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:13.010
Got it, got it.

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:17.770
What are you doing?!

00:06:18.070 --> 00:06:20.050
You didn't need to roll to get that hit!

00:06:20.050 --> 00:06:21.860
Just catch it normally!

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:23.730
S-Sorry!

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:26.420
Nice ball!

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:30.960
<i>His pitches are lively enough.</i>

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:33.170
<i>I just have to make sure
I call a good game.</i>

00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:38.040
<i>I need to make sure my framing 
doesn't go to pot like last time, too.</i>

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:42.580
Shouta!

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:46.710
Oh, you made it!

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:47.540
Yup.

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:49.040
I'm glad we got here in time.

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:51.890
You won your second-round match!
 That's amazing!

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:53.710
Y-Yeah...

00:06:53.710 --> 00:06:56.310
We're rooting for you, 
so bring your A-game, son!

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:57.520
Give it all you've got.

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:58.480
I will!

00:07:02.390 --> 00:07:05.630
Those are pretty fast, but not 
so fast that we can't hit 'em.

00:07:05.630 --> 00:07:06.560
Yeah.

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:09.190
Guess the guy who pitched in 
their last game is their ace.

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:11.700
Mifune

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:11.700
Hongou

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:14.700
Play ball!

00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:16.330
Get 'em, Kimura!

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:17.830
Make sure you get on base!

00:07:21.570 --> 00:07:22.460
Ball.

00:07:23.470 --> 00:07:24.330
Ball.

00:07:25.050 --> 00:07:26.040
Strike!

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:27.920
Ball.

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:29.340
Ball.

00:07:29.910 --> 00:07:31.270
Ball four.

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:37.750
Go, Shigeno-kun!

00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:41.100
Ball.

00:07:42.090 --> 00:07:44.380
<i>Looks like their pitcher isn't warmed up yet.</i>

00:07:44.870 --> 00:07:47.110
<i>We need to score runs 
before he finds his feet.</i>

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:54.720
Out!

00:07:56.750 --> 00:07:57.320
Yeah!

00:07:57.320 --> 00:07:58.580
Nice bunt!

00:07:59.160 --> 00:07:59.950
Yeah!

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:07.450
<i>After that walk, we have a runner 
on second without getting a hit.</i>

00:08:07.870 --> 00:08:09.920
<i>Which means, what he wants most of all is...</i>

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:11.670
<i>...strikes!</i>

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:17.250
Safe!

00:08:17.690 --> 00:08:18.510
All right!

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:22.520
Mifune

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:22.520
Hongou

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:29.590
<i>We can't give this lineup any easy pitches.</i>

00:08:30.490 --> 00:08:33.900
<i>Throw some low outside pitches. 
Let's be meticulous with our aim.</i>

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:40.310
Ball.

00:08:44.050 --> 00:08:44.990
<i>Here, okay?</i>

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:52.550
Ball two!

00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:57.500
<i>Are you okay?</i>

00:08:57.500 --> 00:09:00.180
<i>We can't let the count get any worse.</i>

00:09:01.900 --> 00:09:04.230
<i>High and inside... in the strike zone!</i>

00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:13.350
<i>What's wrong, Hikaru?</i>

00:09:13.790 --> 00:09:15.970
<i>Aren't you feeling it today?</i>

00:09:17.610 --> 00:09:18.200
Ball!

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:19.860
Ball!

00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:21.790
Ball!

00:09:22.450 --> 00:09:23.700
Ball four!

00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:28.750
Hey, now. I thought Satou had 
sorted out his control issues.

00:09:29.070 --> 00:09:30.840
I thought so, too.

00:09:31.730 --> 00:09:33.640
<i>No outs, runners on first and second.</i>

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:34.590
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:09:35.430 --> 00:09:37.470
<i>Maybe my framing's bad?</i>

00:09:37.730 --> 00:09:38.810
<i>Or maybe...</i>

00:09:38.810 --> 00:09:40.890
Huh? This is weird.

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:44.600
Time out, please!

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:49.230
I can go straight down the middle?

00:09:49.460 --> 00:09:50.120
Yeah.

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:54.920
You're holding back your arm because
you're too worried about control.

00:09:55.620 --> 00:09:58.540
So you don't have to worry 
about where to throw it anymore.

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:01.230
Just throw the ball as hard as 
you can, right down the middle!

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:05.200
With your speed, they won't hit you
even if we do that.

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:08.580
Okay. Got it.

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:13.750
Play!

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:15.320
<i>That's right.</i>

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:18.720
<i>What good am I as his catcher
if I don't believe in Hikaru's pitches?</i>

00:10:25.190 --> 00:10:26.220
Strike!

00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:28.190
<i>So fast...</i>

00:10:28.580 --> 00:10:29.770
Nice ball!

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:34.690
Strike two!

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:36.940
Strike! Batter out!

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:38.950
Strike! Out!

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:40.950
Strike! Out!

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:42.320
Yeah!

00:10:42.770 --> 00:10:44.000
Nice pitching.

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:44.950
Thanks!

00:10:50.300 --> 00:10:52.390
All right! One out, runners 
on first and second!

00:10:52.390 --> 00:10:54.380
We've got another chance to score.

00:10:59.060 --> 00:11:00.880
Get us a run, Katsumata-kun!

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:04.260
<i>You're having fun just cheering?</i>

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:07.010
<i>Well, cheerleading's not for me.</i>

00:11:07.010 --> 00:11:09.520
<i>I practiced with my sights 
set on actually playing.</i>

00:11:11.090 --> 00:11:12.420
First!

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:18.300
<i>Two outs, runner on second and third.</i>

00:11:19.340 --> 00:11:20.510
Good luck!

00:11:20.510 --> 00:11:21.320
Now's your chance!

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:23.910
<i>I'm so gonna hit this!</i>

00:11:25.790 --> 00:11:26.910
Strike!

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:29.790
Foul!

00:11:30.770 --> 00:11:31.870
Hit it, Nagai!

00:11:32.150 --> 00:11:33.960
Get those runners home!

00:11:37.080 --> 00:11:38.170
Strike! Out!

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:53.180
I-I'll definitely get a hit next time!

00:11:53.180 --> 00:11:55.180
I won't let you beat me!

00:11:56.180 --> 00:11:57.160
Excuse me?

00:11:57.160 --> 00:11:59.610
What's <i>his</i> problem?

00:12:09.130 --> 00:12:10.160
Strike!

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:11.450
Looking good!

00:12:11.450 --> 00:12:12.960
He's settled into his groove.

00:12:13.240 --> 00:12:14.980
Nice pitching!

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:19.540
Must have been kinda boring sitting 
on the sidelines the whole game, huh?

00:12:19.540 --> 00:12:23.260
Oh, n-no, it wasn't. Just cheering 
everyone on was a lot of fun for me.

00:12:24.060 --> 00:12:25.260
Strike!

00:12:26.220 --> 00:12:29.430
<i>In the beginning, I really meant that.</i>

00:12:29.840 --> 00:12:33.360
<i>But seeing Shigeno-kun and 
the guys having so much fun,</i>

00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:35.400
<i>the baseball-mad side of me 
wanted to be out there.</i>

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:37.400
<i>But then...</i>

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:40.980
There's nothing worse than a talented player 
refusing to live up to their potential!

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:52.330
Mifune

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:52.330
Hongou

00:12:53.340 --> 00:12:54.460
Strike!

00:12:54.640 --> 00:12:58.410
Looks like their pitcher's found 
his rhythm since the third inning.

00:12:58.410 --> 00:12:59.350
Yeah.

00:12:59.350 --> 00:13:03.090
Even though we're leading by one, I wouldn't
mind getting an insurance run soon.

00:13:04.290 --> 00:13:07.850
<i>Just give me another chance.</i>

00:13:08.840 --> 00:13:10.150
All right!

00:13:10.840 --> 00:13:12.110
Out!

00:13:13.410 --> 00:13:15.920
What was that about?!
You need to fight him off more!

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:16.930
Uh, yeah...

00:13:16.930 --> 00:13:17.650
Sorry, dude.

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:20.540
What's Nagai's problem?

00:13:20.540 --> 00:13:21.480
Dunno.

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:26.110
Probably worried he'll lose his spot 
again if he doesn't produce the goods.

00:13:26.260 --> 00:13:27.270
Yeah, guess so.

00:13:28.930 --> 00:13:31.950
Jeez, I hit that traffic jam 
at just the wrong time!

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:33.820
Where's Daigo and the guys?

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:34.660
Huh?

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:38.880
Komori!

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:44.010
The Dolphins should be over on Field C.

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:45.470
Thank you!

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:47.560
Have you only just got here, Shimizu-san?

00:13:47.560 --> 00:13:49.350
Oh, sorry!

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:51.900
Don't sweat it.

00:13:51.900 --> 00:13:56.540
You've always known us as Shimizu Kaoru
and Honda Goro, ever since we were kids.

00:13:57.220 --> 00:13:58.100
Yeah.

00:13:59.110 --> 00:14:03.070
I feel like I've been chasing 
that ball since the moment

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:05.690
I joined the Dolphins 
with you and Honda-kun.

00:14:06.520 --> 00:14:12.080
Even now, I can't escape the lure of 
baseball, so I'm managing a junior team.

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:15.700
I had no idea you were managing a rival team.

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:18.340
In fact, I wanted to thank you 
for all you did for Izumi,

00:14:18.340 --> 00:14:20.460
back when you managed the Dolphins.

00:14:20.460 --> 00:14:21.880
That's not necessary.

00:14:22.270 --> 00:14:26.060
We did everything we could to prepare 
ourselves for a battle with my old team.

00:14:26.060 --> 00:14:28.260
The Dolphins sure were strong!

00:14:28.640 --> 00:14:29.470
Really?

00:14:29.770 --> 00:14:32.360
Daigo-kun's going to be one 
heck of a player someday.

00:14:32.750 --> 00:14:35.720
Toshiya-kun's son also has a lot of talent.

00:14:38.110 --> 00:14:43.050
They're kids who've inherited the talent
of their Major League parents.

00:14:43.050 --> 00:14:45.570
Won't be long before they make
their own mark on the game.

00:14:48.710 --> 00:14:50.720
Here it is. Field C.

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:52.560
Oh, good!

00:14:52.560 --> 00:14:53.540
Thank you.

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:54.430
It's okay.

00:14:54.430 --> 00:14:57.230
Please send my regards to 
Honda-kun in Taiwan, as well.

00:14:57.230 --> 00:14:58.750
I'll tell him you said hello.

00:15:00.260 --> 00:15:03.500
<i>"The kids who've inherited the talent," huh?</i>

00:15:07.460 --> 00:15:10.380
<i>Daigo-kun and his friends aren't
 the only ones with talent, though.</i>

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:22.150
All right!

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:25.230
No outs, runners on second 
and third. Here's our chance!

00:15:25.230 --> 00:15:28.670
<i>I-It's here! I really did get another chance!</i>

00:15:28.670 --> 00:15:29.990
<i>All right!</i>

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:32.460
<i>I really want that run on the board.</i>

00:15:32.460 --> 00:15:33.620
<i>Which means...</i>

00:15:34.290 --> 00:15:36.490
Sakura will be pinch-hitting for Nagai.

00:15:47.080 --> 00:15:47.810
Bah!

00:15:49.700 --> 00:15:50.670
I promise I'll hit it!

00:15:52.560 --> 00:15:54.200
For your sake, too...

00:15:55.090 --> 00:15:56.710
Because I don't want to lose.

00:15:56.710 --> 00:15:59.720
Because I want to play the 
next match with everyone.

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:02.750
Because I'm a member of the Dolphins!

00:16:11.110 --> 00:16:12.530
Go, Sakura!

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:14.110
Mutsuko-chan! Fight!

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:17.740
Strike!

00:16:18.210 --> 00:16:21.730
<i>Damn it. What the hell do you 
mean, for my sake, too?</i>

00:16:21.730 --> 00:16:24.000
<i>I'll get my </i>own<i> hits, thank you very much!</i>

00:16:24.950 --> 00:16:25.750
Ball.

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:26.590
Well done!

00:16:26.590 --> 00:16:27.770
Stay sharp!

00:16:27.770 --> 00:16:29.270
You can hit this!

00:16:29.270 --> 00:16:33.220
<i>The next chance I get, I'm really gonna...</i>

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:35.840
<i>So come on!</i>

00:16:37.300 --> 00:16:39.910
Hit it, Sakura!

00:16:56.610 --> 00:16:57.980
Yeah!

00:16:59.190 --> 00:17:02.410
<i>Damn it! How can she hit it like that?!</i>

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:04.910
Mifune

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:04.910
Hongou

00:17:09.780 --> 00:17:11.090
Strike! Out!

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:12.630
That's game.

00:17:12.630 --> 00:17:14.380
We won!

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:15.860
We won...

00:17:15.860 --> 00:17:17.350
We won again!

00:17:17.350 --> 00:17:18.930
We're in the quarterfinals!

00:17:25.720 --> 00:17:27.220
Hello? Mayumura here.

00:17:27.220 --> 00:17:29.690
<i>Hey, where are you? 
The game's about to start.</i>

00:17:30.270 --> 00:17:32.410
Yes, I'll be right there.

00:17:34.420 --> 00:17:36.980
He shut out the Sharks' offense,
giving up only two hits.

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:39.880
Just who is that kid with the glasses?

00:17:41.190 --> 00:17:43.660
You guys were something else.

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:46.120
But I have to say, Satou was the real MVP.

00:17:46.120 --> 00:17:50.420
You only gave them two walks and 
two singles. That's some fine pitching!

00:17:50.790 --> 00:17:54.290
Nah, it's Daigo-kun who 
deserves all the plaudits.

00:17:54.870 --> 00:17:58.800
He stayed focused to the end and caught 
every single ball with proper framing.

00:17:59.080 --> 00:18:00.640
Of course!

00:18:00.820 --> 00:18:02.610
You did a great job, too, Daigo!

00:18:04.800 --> 00:18:07.190
Looks like we're finally 
gonna play the Touto Boys.

00:18:07.190 --> 00:18:07.980
Yeah.

00:18:08.360 --> 00:18:13.230
Honestly, Satou's homer and his sickening
baseball instincts get my back up.

00:18:13.230 --> 00:18:16.590
You guys were really amazing out there.

00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:18.150
But if it wasn't for him, we wouldn't have 
made it to the quarterfinals so easily.

00:18:16.590 --> 00:18:17.960
You weren't too bad, Daigo-kun.

00:18:19.970 --> 00:18:22.240
Our dream of beating the Touto Boys isn't—

00:18:23.920 --> 00:18:24.970
Wait, that's...

00:18:27.700 --> 00:18:29.180
Hey, where are you going?

00:18:29.180 --> 00:18:29.990
Toilet.

00:18:29.990 --> 00:18:31.290
I'll be right back.

00:18:33.100 --> 00:18:37.010
Daigo! Congratulations!

00:18:37.270 --> 00:18:39.920
I can't believe you won two games 
in one day! That is <i>so</i> amazing!

00:18:39.920 --> 00:18:41.470
Ack! Let go!

00:18:41.470 --> 00:18:43.180
Why? I'm praising you!

00:18:43.180 --> 00:18:44.720
Let go of me!

00:18:45.020 --> 00:18:47.340
Besides, I didn't do anything!

00:18:47.340 --> 00:18:48.050
Huh?

00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:51.300
I got switched out in the 
middle of the first game,

00:18:51.720 --> 00:18:55.730
and in this game, Hikaru just threw
 balls that were easy for me to catch.

00:18:56.530 --> 00:19:00.450
Our team won, but all I did was 
add to my list of things to improve.

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:04.550
Wow, what a selfless child!

00:19:04.550 --> 00:19:06.570
He must have wonderful parents!

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:10.800
Please get everyone together 
and head home without me.

00:19:10.800 --> 00:19:11.630
What?

00:19:11.630 --> 00:19:13.560
Are you going scouting? 
Maybe we should all come—

00:19:13.560 --> 00:19:16.670
No. Touto's on a whole other level.

00:19:17.120 --> 00:19:19.470
If they see them play, 
our kids will lose hope.

00:19:20.250 --> 00:19:22.470
I see. I hear you.

00:19:23.560 --> 00:19:24.600
Mayumura!

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:29.020
Oh, it's you.

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:31.650
I forget your name...

00:19:31.650 --> 00:19:32.850
Andy, isn't it?

00:19:33.340 --> 00:19:35.510
No, it <i>isn't</i>! I'm Urabe. Urabe!

00:19:35.510 --> 00:19:37.480
Urabe? Oh, yeah, so it is.

00:19:38.140 --> 00:19:42.610
Part of that weak battery that ran away
and joined the Dolphins in fifth grade.

00:19:43.870 --> 00:19:46.000
I-I didn't run away!

00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:48.240
Well, that's what everyone on the team said.

00:19:48.480 --> 00:19:49.710
That's crap and you know it!

00:19:49.710 --> 00:19:53.910
Andy and I joined the Dolphins 
so we could crush you guys.

00:19:54.770 --> 00:19:57.370
So that makes you the Dolphins' ace, right?

00:19:57.370 --> 00:19:58.460
You better believe it!

00:19:58.900 --> 00:20:00.230
That's pretty impressive.

00:20:00.740 --> 00:20:05.350
So Specs, who threw monster fastballs 
in that last game, is your relief pitcher?

00:20:05.860 --> 00:20:09.050
You're telling me you're 
a better pitcher than him?

00:20:09.550 --> 00:20:11.210
W-Well...

00:20:11.210 --> 00:20:14.850
Whatever. That kid in the glasses is 
a rookie who only just started playing.

00:20:15.300 --> 00:20:17.440
He's... a rookie?

00:20:17.730 --> 00:20:20.960
Urabe! What are you doing over here?

00:20:20.960 --> 00:20:21.950
U-Uh, nothing.

00:20:22.390 --> 00:20:24.780
Oh, right. I can't stick around.

00:20:24.780 --> 00:20:26.530
I've got a game to get to.

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:28.950
If we win, we'll be playing the Dolphins.

00:20:29.430 --> 00:20:31.960
Guess that means you'll be rooting for us.

00:20:32.990 --> 00:20:35.340
H-Hey, Mayumura! Wait!

00:20:35.340 --> 00:20:37.740
Aren't you Touto's ace?

00:20:37.740 --> 00:20:39.820
Why are you wearing the number two jersey?

00:20:42.410 --> 00:20:44.760
Because I'm the catcher, of course.

00:20:45.580 --> 00:20:47.700
I'm not the pitcher.

00:20:49.520 --> 00:20:51.980
Wh-What did he say?

00:20:53.700 --> 00:20:55.810
Where the heck has Urabe got to?

00:20:56.170 --> 00:20:57.090
Coach?

00:20:57.090 --> 00:21:01.760
Has our manager gone to 
check out the Touto Boys?

00:21:01.760 --> 00:21:03.250
Maybe that's where Urabe went, too.

00:21:03.250 --> 00:21:05.410
U-Uh, who knows?

00:21:05.770 --> 00:21:07.310
I know.

00:21:07.310 --> 00:21:10.700
He didn't want us to see them play, 
because we'd lose all hope if we did, right?

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:11.240
Beats me...

00:21:11.720 --> 00:21:14.400
What? It's fine. We should go watch them!

00:21:14.400 --> 00:21:16.110
We won't know until we see for ourselves.

00:21:16.110 --> 00:21:16.820
Uh, I don't know.

00:21:16.820 --> 00:21:17.750
What do you all say?

00:21:17.970 --> 00:21:19.200
Let's do it!

00:21:19.200 --> 00:21:20.970
We don't lose anything by just spectating.

00:21:20.970 --> 00:21:22.480
Let's go, Coach!

00:21:23.200 --> 00:21:25.590
We've made it to the quarterfinals.

00:21:25.810 --> 00:21:27.430
If we're going to freak out anyway,

00:21:27.430 --> 00:21:29.510
it's better to do it before the game!

00:21:29.510 --> 00:21:30.890
We need to throw everything at them!

00:21:31.590 --> 00:21:33.640
S-Sure...

00:21:42.650 --> 00:21:45.150
Touto

00:21:45.860 --> 00:21:47.700
So that's Touto's cleanup?

00:21:48.450 --> 00:21:52.600
That's Mayumura Wataru, the son of 
Major League player, Mayumura Ken.

00:21:53.110 --> 00:21:55.730
Oh, there's Touto's ace.

00:22:00.530 --> 00:22:02.210
Y-You've gotta be kidding.

00:22:08.080 --> 00:22:10.050
<i>Th-That girl...</i>

00:22:17.250 --> 00:22:18.600
<i>That time in the cages...</i>

00:22:19.410 --> 00:22:22.000
She's Wataru's twin sister.

00:22:26.990 --> 00:22:28.710
Mayumura Michiru.

00:24:01.160 --> 00:24:03.080
So Mayumura Junior has a twin?

00:24:03.080 --> 00:24:05.500
And she's their ace?

00:24:05.950 --> 00:24:09.690
We've got to defeat those siblings 
if we want to beat the Touto Boys.

00:24:09.690 --> 00:24:12.970
Hold on a minute! Why's she in my house?!

00:24:13.750 --> 00:24:15.870
This is my chance.

00:24:14.550 --> 00:24:18.010
Resignation

00:24:16.300 --> 00:24:18.690
No, wait, this is bad.

00:24:18.010 --> 00:24:24.980
The Mayumura Siblings

00:24:19.110 --> 00:24:21.560
Next time: "The Mayumura Siblings"

00:24:21.560 --> 00:24:23.690
Run to the stage of your dreams!
